WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.529
Step 1. Open the Immunizations tab of the encounter.

1.2
00:00:03.529 --> 00:00:07.879
Applying a policy adds its recommendations to the patient's schedule.

1.3
00:00:07.879 --> 00:00:13.486
Open the patient's encounter from your facility and select the Immunizations tab.

2.1
00:00:13.486 --> 00:00:19.135
Step 2. Open the Apply policy dialog. Select Apply policy at the top of the panel.

2.2
00:00:19.135 --> 00:00:24.574
Care shows it only in an open encounter that you opened from your facility.

3.1
00:00:24.574 --> 00:00:26.558
Step 3. Select the policy.

3.2
00:00:26.558 --> 00:00:31.760
The Policy list shows the policies of your facility and the instance policies,

3.3
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.595
by name. Select the policy that you want to apply.

4.1
00:00:35.595 --> 00:00:37.810
Step 4. Check the start date.

4.2
00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:41.672
Care counts the day offsets of the policy from this date.

4.3
00:00:41.672 --> 00:00:46.577
It defaults to the date of birth, so here you change it to today.

5.1
00:00:46.577 --> 00:00:49.335
Step 5. Review the schedule preview.

5.2
00:00:49.335 --> 00:00:54.212
Each row shows the vaccine, the series and the dose, and its due date.

5.3
00:00:54.212 --> 00:00:59.379
Care adds only these recommendations, not the groups of the policy.

6.1
00:00:59.379 --> 00:01:04.062
Step 6. Add the recommendations. Select Add 3 recommendations.

6.2
00:01:04.062 --> 00:01:06.850
Care shows Immunization policy applied,

6.3
00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:12.498
and the new recommendations appear in the Schedule as Upcoming, Due or Overdue,

6.4
00:01:12.498 --> 00:01:14.214
from their dates.
